00:47:54.980 --> 00:47:57.020
I would have loved to have seen their wedding.
我本来很想看他们的婚礼。

1088
00:47:57.480 --> 00:47:59.800
Because, you know, Michael's going to be Bridezilla.
因为你知道，迈克尔肯定会是个“新郎zilla”。

1089
00:48:00.680 --> 00:48:01.380
You think?
你觉得呢？

1090
00:48:01.700 --> 00:48:02.100
Yes.
是的。

1091
00:48:02.220 --> 00:48:04.360
And I think Holly's just going to let him have his moment.
而且我觉得霍莉只会让他尽情享受那一刻。

1092
00:48:04.460 --> 00:48:08.100
But I think Michael's going to have really strong feelings about his wedding day.
但我认为迈克尔对自己的婚礼当天会有非常强烈的执念。

1093
00:48:08.400 --> 00:48:11.840
Do you think they would have traded vows, like in a Yoda voice?
你觉得他们会用尤达大师的口吻交换誓词吗？

1094
00:48:12.340 --> 00:48:16.180
Oh, I think they would have for sure written their own vows.
哦，我觉得他们肯定会自己写誓词。

1095
00:48:16.340 --> 00:48:19.200
Which I would have just loved to hear.
我真的很想听听看。

1096
00:48:19.200 --> 00:48:24.840
Oh, Mindy, Mindy Kaling, can we call her and be like, will you write these right now so we can read them on the podcast?
哦，明迪，明迪·卡灵，我们能给她打电话说：“你现在能写出来吗？这样我们就能在播客上读给大家听了。”

1097
00:48:25.360 --> 00:48:32.380
Yeah, I think at some point in the wedding vows, there would have been some type of, like, accents, character impersonations.
是啊，我觉得在婚礼誓词的某个环节，肯定会有某种口音或角色模仿。

1098
00:48:32.700 --> 00:48:32.940
Yes.
没错。

1099
00:48:33.160 --> 00:48:33.800
Things like that.
诸如此类的东西。

1100
00:48:33.960 --> 00:48:38.400
I feel like there would have been maybe some, like, Princess Bride references.
我觉得可能还会有些像《公主新娘》那样的梗。

1101
00:48:39.040 --> 00:48:39.160
Oh.
噢。

1102
00:48:39.180 --> 00:48:40.080
Like, marriage.
比如，婚姻。

1103
00:48:40.440 --> 00:48:40.840
Marriage.
婚姻。

1104
00:48:41.540 --> 00:48:42.800
Brings us together.
把我们聚在一起。

1105
00:48:43.720 --> 00:48:44.080
Yeah.
是啊。

1106
00:48:44.420 --> 00:48:44.600
Yeah.
没错。

1107
00:48:44.900 --> 00:48:46.060
The holy spigot.
神圣的源泉。

1108
00:48:46.520 --> 00:48:46.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1109
00:48:46.840 --> 00:48:46.980
Yeah.
没错。

1110
00:48:47.900 --> 00:48:48.820
For sure.
确实。

1111
00:48:49.200 --> 00:48:49.860
I don't know.
我不知道。

1112
00:48:50.080 --> 00:48:51.700
There just would have been a lot of voices.
当时会有很多不同的声音。

1113
00:48:52.640 --> 00:48:53.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1114
00:48:53.340 --> 00:48:54.620
Marry you, I will.
我会娶你的。

1115
00:48:54.900 --> 00:48:55.740
Yeah, there you go.
对，就是这样。

1116
00:48:55.880 --> 00:48:57.220
But it would have been really joyous.
但那一定会非常欢乐。

1117
00:48:57.340 --> 00:48:59.680
We'll tell you why it didn't happen.
我们会告诉你为什么没能实现。

1118
00:48:59.680 --> 00:49:05.880
It was because, first of all, Steve Carell was no longer under contract with the show, you know?
首先是因为，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔当时已经不再和剧组续约了，你知道吧？

1119
00:49:06.040 --> 00:49:08.960
Michael marries Holly somewhere in season eight or nine.
迈克尔在第八或第九季的某个时候娶了霍莉。

1120
00:49:08.960 --> 00:49:12.180
When he shows up for the finale, you know, it's years later.
当他在大结局出现时，已经是多年以后了。

1121
00:49:12.180 --> 00:49:14.900
So that wedding happened off camera.
所以那场婚礼是在镜头外举行的。

1122
00:49:14.940 --> 00:49:19.720
But both Amy and Steve had already left the show and were doing other things.
但艾米和史蒂夫当时都已经离开了剧组，在忙别的事情。

1123
00:49:19.740 --> 00:49:22.080
And so we just didn't get to see their wedding.
所以我们没能看到他们的婚礼。

1124
00:49:22.200 --> 00:49:24.180
But man, I so wish that we could have.
但天哪，我真希望我们能看到。

1125
00:49:24.500 --> 00:49:24.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1126
00:49:25.680 --> 00:49:28.860
I mean, I think he would have had to make Dwight his best man.
我是说，我觉得他肯定得让德怀特当伴郎。

1127
00:49:29.860 --> 00:49:30.560
You think?
你觉得呢？

1128
00:49:31.000 --> 00:49:31.360
Yeah.
是的。

1129
00:49:31.500 --> 00:49:36.480
He wouldn't have tried to make, like, Ryan his best man or Danny Cordray or one of the
他难道不会试着让瑞安，或者丹尼·科德雷，或者其他那些

1130
00:49:36.480 --> 00:49:37.980
last handsome ones.
最后剩下的帅哥当伴郎吗？

1131
00:49:38.100 --> 00:49:39.060
He would have tried.
他肯定会试的。

1132
00:49:39.060 --> 00:49:43.060
And, but I think it would have ended up being Dwight.
但是，我觉得最后还是会变成德怀特。

1133
00:49:43.260 --> 00:49:43.720
I do.
我也这么觉得。

1134
00:49:43.940 --> 00:49:44.340
You do?
你真的这么想？

1135
00:49:44.580 --> 00:49:44.820
Yeah.
是的。

1136
00:49:44.960 --> 00:49:48.300
Because he would have taken care of Michael and made sure it was all of Michael's favorite
因为他会照顾好迈克尔，确保婚礼上全是迈克尔最喜欢的

1137
00:49:48.300 --> 00:49:48.640
things.
东西。

1138
00:49:48.820 --> 00:49:51.820
But there would have been at least one moment where he went too big.
但肯定会有那么一刻，他会搞得太夸张。

1139
00:49:52.400 --> 00:49:54.340
And Michael would have been like, damn it, Dwight.
然后迈克尔就会说，该死，德怀特。

1140
00:49:54.500 --> 00:49:57.780
I think there might have been a full choir that sings.
我觉得可能还会有一个完整的唱诗班在唱歌。

1141
00:49:58.500 --> 00:49:59.480
I could see that.
我能想象那个画面。

1142
00:49:59.680 --> 00:49:59.860
Right?
对吧？

1143
00:50:00.180 --> 00:50:00.380
Yeah.
是啊。

1144
00:50:00.920 --> 00:50:01.240
Yeah.
没错。

1145
00:50:01.480 --> 00:50:03.580
They would have done the cut the cake thing.
他们肯定会搞切蛋糕那一套。

1146
00:50:03.840 --> 00:50:05.080
And they're both such dorks.
而且他们俩都是那种呆子。

1147
00:50:05.200 --> 00:50:05.800
The cake theme.
蛋糕的主题。

1148
00:50:05.940 --> 00:50:06.960
What would the cake have been?
蛋糕会是什么样的呢？

1149
00:50:07.400 --> 00:50:08.900
Oh, that's a good question.
噢，这是个好问题。

1150
00:50:09.060 --> 00:50:12.140
Just all the little touches would have been so fun.
所有那些小细节一定会非常有趣。

1151
00:50:12.340 --> 00:50:12.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1152
00:50:12.640 --> 00:50:13.280
It's too bad.
真可惜。

1153
00:50:13.500 --> 00:50:14.720
Oh, you know what I think?
噢，你知道我在想什么吗？

1154
00:50:14.840 --> 00:50:15.480
Last thing.
最后一点。

1155
00:50:15.700 --> 00:50:20.060
Because now I'm just so excited, just kind of envisioning the Michael and Holly wedding.
因为我现在太兴奋了，脑子里已经在构想迈克尔和霍莉的婚礼了。

1156
00:50:20.200 --> 00:50:26.480
I think for sure the two of them would have spent weeks working on a choreographed first
我觉得他们俩肯定会花上几周时间排练一段精心编排的开场

1157
00:50:26.480 --> 00:50:27.020
dance.
舞。

1158
00:50:27.220 --> 00:50:27.620
Yes.
没错。

1159
00:50:27.620 --> 00:50:30.060
That they would have performed for everyone.
那是他们会表演给所有人看的。

1160
00:50:30.320 --> 00:50:30.720
Yes.
是的。

1161
00:50:31.080 --> 00:50:35.980
But I also think Michael would have insisted that everybody lift him up on a chair,
但我还觉得迈克尔会坚持让大家把他抬到椅子上，

1162
00:50:36.160 --> 00:50:38.620
even though it was not a Jewish wedding.
尽管那根本不是犹太婚礼。

1163
00:50:38.620 --> 00:50:39.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1164
00:50:39.180 --> 00:50:40.680
He would have wanted that tradition.
他就是会想要那种传统。

1165
00:50:41.000 --> 00:50:41.260
The moment.
那种时刻。

1166
00:50:41.520 --> 00:50:41.920
Yes.
没错。

1167
00:50:42.060 --> 00:50:44.180
Because he had seen it in a movie or something.
因为他可能在电影里还是哪儿见过。

1168
00:50:44.620 --> 00:50:51.800
Or they would have like entered their reception in like a ye olde carriage or something.
或者他们会坐着那种老式马车之类的东西入场。

1169
00:50:52.220 --> 00:50:57.640
I was at a wedding one time where the bride and groom entered in a horse-drawn carriage.
我以前参加过一个婚礼，新郎新娘就是坐着马车入场的。

1170
00:50:57.960 --> 00:50:59.920
They entered the indoors?
他们坐进室内了？

1171
00:51:00.320 --> 00:51:01.620
Like a Cinderella carriage.
就像灰姑娘那种马车。

1172
00:51:01.620 --> 00:51:03.160
They entered a ballroom.
他们进了宴会厅。

1173
00:51:03.300 --> 00:51:04.620
It was on the first floor.
就在一楼。

1174
00:51:05.160 --> 00:51:11.820
With one horse pulling like a little Cinderella round wrought iron carriage that they sat in.
一匹马拉着那种小小的、圆形的锻铁马车，他们就坐在里面。

1175
00:51:11.960 --> 00:51:13.100
Do I know these people?
我认识这些人吗？

1176
00:51:13.300 --> 00:51:13.600
No.
不认识。

1177
00:51:13.880 --> 00:51:14.180
No.
不认识。

1178
00:51:14.320 --> 00:51:16.880
This was a huge Dallas, Texas wedding.
那是在得克萨斯州达拉斯举办的一场盛大婚礼。

1179
00:51:17.500 --> 00:51:18.020
Wow.
哇。

1180
00:51:18.260 --> 00:51:18.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1181
00:51:18.720 --> 00:51:23.200
And I literally like the big doors open and then you're like clip, clop, clip.
我当时真的就是，大门一开，然后就听到哒哒、哒哒的声音。

1182
00:51:23.420 --> 00:51:24.580
I was like, what is happening?
我当时心想，这是在干嘛？

1183
00:51:25.600 --> 00:51:26.920
Am I an old lady?
我是变成老太太了吗？

1184
00:51:26.940 --> 00:51:30.080
Because when I hear that, I think, oh, what a waste of money.
因为听到那个声音，我只会想，噢，真是浪费钱。

1185
00:51:30.580 --> 00:51:30.900
No.
可不是嘛。

1186
00:51:31.220 --> 00:51:31.740
You know what?
你知道吗？

1187
00:51:31.940 --> 00:51:32.860
You know what?
你知道吗？

1188
00:51:32.960 --> 00:51:35.440
Use that for some good bed linens.
把那些钱花在好的床上用品上多好。

1189
00:51:35.800 --> 00:51:36.020
Well.
嗯。

1190
00:51:36.580 --> 00:51:37.620
You know what?
你知道吗？

1191
00:51:37.720 --> 00:51:39.080
Double up on all your sheets.
多买几套好床单。

1192
00:51:39.200 --> 00:51:41.280
That's a better way to spend your money on it.
那才是更好的花钱方式。

1193
00:51:41.420 --> 00:51:43.260
Get the good towels.
买点好的毛巾。

1194
00:51:43.640 --> 00:51:43.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1195
00:51:44.000 --> 00:51:44.420
Exactly.
没错。

1196
00:51:44.900 --> 00:51:45.680
That carriage.
至于那马车。

1197
00:51:45.880 --> 00:51:47.600
I'm like, you'll use the towels forever.
我觉得，毛巾你可是能用一辈子的。

1198
00:51:47.600 --> 00:51:48.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1199
00:51:48.440 --> 00:51:52.720
Also, you know, the number of mishaps that can happen getting in and out of that carriage
而且，你知道，穿着礼服、踩着高跟鞋上下那种马车，

1200
00:51:52.720 --> 00:51:54.620
in your dress with your fancy shoes.
可能会出多少岔子啊。

1201
00:51:54.820 --> 00:51:55.200
Yeah.
没错。

1202
00:51:55.460 --> 00:51:56.260
Go get the towels.
去拿毛巾吧。

1203
00:51:56.880 --> 00:51:58.260
We're practical ladies.
我们是很务实的女性。

1204
00:51:58.500 --> 00:51:59.000
We are.
确实如此。

1205
00:51:59.440 --> 00:52:03.100
But also, if you want a carriage at your wedding, you do you.
但话说回来，如果你婚礼上想要马车，那你就随心所欲吧。

1206
00:52:03.380 --> 00:52:04.340
Yes, that's right.
是的，没错。

1207
00:52:04.960 --> 00:52:05.840
I don't judge.
我不会评判。

1208
00:52:05.840 --> 00:52:06.900
I just can't relate.
我只是无法感同身受。

1209
00:52:07.860 --> 00:52:08.780
It's different.
这不一样。

1210
00:52:09.080 --> 00:52:10.380
Stitch that on a pillow.
把这句话绣在枕头上吧。

1211
00:52:10.860 --> 00:52:11.760
I don't judge.
我不会评判。

1212
00:52:11.760 --> 00:52:15.340
I just can't relate is actually a really great pillow.
“我只是无法感同身受”这枕头标语真的很棒。

1213
00:52:15.740 --> 00:52:16.080
It is.
确实。

1214
00:52:17.900 --> 00:52:20.800
Oh, well, you guys, this has been really great.
噢，好吧，各位，今天真是太棒了。

1215
00:52:21.200 --> 00:52:21.860
Thank you.
谢谢你们。

1216
00:52:22.020 --> 00:52:23.080
I feel so celebrated.
我感觉受到了隆重的庆祝。

1217
00:52:23.280 --> 00:52:25.480
Angela, when your birthday comes up, we're going to have to do the same thing.
安吉拉，等你生日的时候，我们也得如法炮制。

1218
00:52:25.600 --> 00:52:27.440
You have to answer the call sheet questions now.
你现在得回答那些通告单上的问题了。

1219
00:52:27.620 --> 00:52:28.680
It was your idea.
这是你的主意。

1220
00:52:28.840 --> 00:52:29.700
You started it.
是你先开始的。

1221
00:52:29.860 --> 00:52:30.140
Okay.
好吧。

1222
00:52:30.240 --> 00:52:31.320
Now you have to do it.
现在你必须得做了。

1223
00:52:31.460 --> 00:52:31.960
Oh, great.
噢，太好了。

1224
00:52:32.300 --> 00:52:32.700
All right.
行吧。

1225
00:52:32.900 --> 00:52:34.200
Sam, Matt, one of your birthdays.
萨姆，马特，你们俩谁的生日快到了。

1226
00:52:35.040 --> 00:52:36.780
I'm not the only one doing this.
不能只有我一个人做这事。

1227
00:52:37.500 --> 00:52:43.460
And maybe we'll come up with some tribute to you that's like, I'm thinking maybe tennis
也许我们会为你准备一个致敬环节，我在想，也许是网球

1228
00:52:43.460 --> 00:52:43.920
related.
主题的。

1229
00:52:44.240 --> 00:52:46.980
Do we have to share our favorite tennis moment from history?
我们得分享各自历史上最喜欢的网球时刻吗？

1230
00:52:47.600 --> 00:52:49.040
Mine was a surprise to you.
我那个时刻对你来说是个惊喜。

1231
00:52:49.180 --> 00:52:49.440
Okay.
好吧。

1232
00:52:49.440 --> 00:52:50.980
Our shared moment was a surprise.
我们共同的时刻是一个惊喜。

1233
00:52:51.080 --> 00:52:52.080
You have to surprise me.
你得给我惊喜。

1234
00:52:52.200 --> 00:52:52.420
Okay.
好吧。

1235
00:52:52.600 --> 00:52:53.440
I don't want to know.
我不想提前知道。

1236
00:52:53.600 --> 00:52:53.840
Okay.
好吧。

1237
00:52:54.040 --> 00:52:55.620
But I get to pick my own theme, lady.
但我可以自己选主题，女士。

1238
00:52:55.740 --> 00:52:57.040
You don't get to pick my birthday theme.
你不能替我选生日主题。

1239
00:52:57.040 --> 00:52:57.340
Okay.
好吧。

1240
00:52:57.460 --> 00:53:00.440
You pick your theme and then that will point us in a direction.
你选好主题，然后我们就会朝着那个方向准备。

1241
00:53:00.440 --> 00:53:01.100
I like it.
我喜欢这个主意。

1242
00:53:01.240 --> 00:53:01.480
Okay.
好的。

1243
00:53:01.680 --> 00:53:02.900
Well, thank you, everybody.
那么，谢谢大家。

1244
00:53:03.140 --> 00:53:04.160
This was really fun.
这真的很有趣。

1245
00:53:04.380 --> 00:53:04.840
All right.
好的。

1246
00:53:05.060 --> 00:53:06.300
We'll see you guys next week.
我们下周见。

1247
00:53:06.360 --> 00:53:07.320
We hope you had a great one.
希望你们度过了愉快的一周。

1248
00:53:07.460 --> 00:53:08.340
Thanks for writing in.
感谢你们的来信。

1249
00:53:08.420 --> 00:53:09.880
We appreciate you all so much.
我们非常感激大家。

1250
00:53:10.020 --> 00:53:10.660
See you next week.
下周见。

1251
00:53:10.660 --> 00:53:16.070
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

